1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,500
Creator samples are a second fulfilment stream.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,100
Nobody plans it.

3
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:06,300
Everyone plans the regular orders.

4
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,100
Nobody plans the creator samples.

5
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:11,100
Different packaging: no receipt, no price, and it has to look good on an unboxing camera.

6
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:14,100
Different deadline: the creator needs it fast, while the trend is alive.

7
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:16,600
Same parcel, different job.

8
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,400
The invoice comes out. The price comes off.

9
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:22,400
It gets packed to look good on camera, and tagged as a creator sample.

10
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,100
Then it joins the sample stream.

11
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,000
Then an agency sends one request:

12
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
fifty creator samples.

13
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:33,300
50 creators. 50 micro-orders. Overnight.

14
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:38,000
If you run an agency pushing creator samples, DM me.

